      "answer": "B",
      "explanationEn": "B is correct. Insurers are double exposed to climate risks because both sides of their balance sheet can be affected by these risks. On the liability side, property and casualty insurers face physical climate risks, such as increased frequency and severity of natural disasters. On the asset side, climate risks affect insurers’ portfolios as the assets are repriced.",
      "explanationZh": "B 正确。保险公司对气候风险具有双重暴露，因为其资产负债表两端都可能受到这些风险影响。在负债端，财产和意外险公司面临实体气候风险，例如自然灾害发生频率和严重程度上升。在资产端，随着资产重新定价，气候风险会影响保险公司的投资组合。",
