      "answer": "A",
      "explanationEn": "A is correct. In Germany, most board structures are two-tier, whereby supervisory and management boards are separate and responsible for different functions. In Japan, statutory auditors and single-tier boards prevail. In both countries, there is a tendency for dominance by major shareholders in leading companies rather than having more diversified ownership of companies with many smaller shareholders. Independent audit firms are a requirement for companies in both countries.",
      "explanationZh": "A 正确。在德国，多数董事会结构为双层结构，即监督董事会和管理董事会分离，并负责不同职能。在日本，法定审计人和单层董事会占主导。在两个国家，领先公司都倾向于由主要股东主导，而不是由许多较小股东组成的更分散所有权结构。独立审计 firm 是两国公司的要求。",
      "keywordEn": "Japan vs Germany -> single-tier versus two-tier boards",
