      "explanationEn": "B is correct. According to the ICGN Global Governance Principles, investors might question the independence of directors who used to be executives of the company if there “was not an appropriate gap between their employment and joining the board.” Independence might be questioned if directors’ tenures are too long, usually over 10 years, but some countries’ codes might limit maximum tenures to as little as 5 to 7 years. A tenure of 3 years would not raise questions absent other information. There is no principle of questioning independence where the board member was recruited from competitors.",
      "explanationZh": "B 正确。根据 ICGN 全球治理原则，如果曾担任公司高管的董事在离职和加入董事会之间“没有适当间隔”，投资者可能质疑其独立性。如果董事任期过长，通常超过 10 年，也可能受到质疑，但一些国家的治理代码可能将最长任期限制为短至 5 至 7 年。在没有其他信息的情况下，3 年任期不会引发质疑。没有原则认为从竞争对手处招聘的董事会成员应被质疑独立性。",
