      "answer": "A",
      "explanationEn": "A is correct. When there are concerns about a company’s financial viability, investors will carefully consider their votes on dividends, as dividends would further constrain the company’s cash resources.",
      "explanationZh": "A 正确。当对公司财务可行性存在担忧时，投资者会仔细考虑其关于股利的投票，因为股利会进一步限制公司的现金资源。",
      "keywordEn": "financial viability + cash resources → dividends",
      "reverseZh": "看到 financial viability 和现金资源压力，反推 dividends。",
      "trap": "审计师薪酬和董事连任不如股利直接影响现金资源。",
      "link": "ch06/esg_ch6_three_round_practice.html",
      "hasAnswer": true,
