      "link": "",
      "hasAnswer": true,
      "hasExplanation": true,
      "rawText": "The decoupling of economic activities from resource usage means?\nA. Transition from a linear to a circular economy\nB. Transition from a circular to a linear economy\nC. More raw resources used\nTo a certain degree, technological innovation and moving from a linear to a circular economy has the potential to reduce the need for virgin resources. The decoupling of economic activities from resource usage has been observed; for example, between 2010 and 2022, global GDP per capita has risen by over 20% while carbon emissions per capita have fallen by about 2%,\n在一定程度上，技术创新以及从线性经济转向循环经济，有潜力降低对原生资源的需求。经济活动与资源使用之间的脱钩已经被观察到；例如，2010 年至 2022 年间，全球人均 GDP 上升超过 20%，而人均碳排放下降约 2%。",
      "knowledgePoint": "Decoupling"
