      "link": "",
      "hasAnswer": true,
      "hasExplanation": true,
      "rawText": "What does the Jevons paradox refer to, as described in the passage?\nA. Increased resource efficiency leading to a proportional decrease in total resource consumption of a product\nB. Relative improvements in production efficiency (using fewer resources per unit) being offset by higher consumption of a given product\nC. The shift from a linear to a circular economic model to reduce strain on natural resources\nOne reason is that relative improvements in efficiency (using fewer resources per unit of production) may be offset by increased consumption of a given product-an effect known as the Jevons paradox The issue of resource usage will remain crucial for investors and policymakers, who will have to navigate trade-offs and consider not just use efficiency but also how to facilitate changing the whole model (moving from linear to circular in products, processes, and, ultimately, the economy) to reduce the strain on natural resources.\n原因之一是，效率的相对提升（单位产出使用更少资源）可能会被某一产品消费量的增加所抵消，这种效应被称为杰文斯悖论。资源使用问题对投资者和政策制定者仍将至关重要，他们必须权衡取舍，不仅考虑使用效率，还要考虑如何推动整个模式转变，即在产品、流程乃至最终经济层面从线性转向循环，以减少对自然资源的压力。",
