      "rawText": "Successful investor engagement tends to have the most positive impact:\nA. On restructuring and financial policies.\nB. On changes to remuneration policies.\nC. Within six months of the initial engagement contact.\nTo assess this, the authors sought to identify engagement success by analyzing the objectives that were set for each engagement at the start. They found that most of the stated objectives were achieved, with a 65% success rate overall, with the greatest success in restructuring and financial policies and slightly less success with regard to board change. Ironically perhaps, the lowest success rate was found in areas where shareholder engagement occurs more frequently, with only 25% of the desired remuneration policy changes achieved and only 44% of the desired improvements to investor relations achieved. While analyzing this success, the authors also found that the fund achieved positive financial returns. At the time, the fund’s overall performance (net of fees) was 4.9% more than the FTSE All-Share Performance. Out of this excess return, 90% was attributed to activist outcomes.\n为了评估这一点，作者通过分析每次参与沟通开始时设定的目标，识别参与沟通是否成功。他们发现，大多数既定目标得以实现，整体成功率为 65%；其中重组和财务政策方面最成功，董事会变更方面的成功略低。或许有些讽刺的是，最低成功率出现在股东参与最频繁的领域：期望的薪酬政策变化仅有 25% 实现，期望的投资者关系改善仅有 44% 实现。在分析这种成功时，作者还发现该基金取得了正的财务回报。当时，该基金整体表现（扣除费用后）比 FTSE All-Share Performance 高 4.9%。在这部分超额回报中，90% 归因于积极主义结果。",
