      "answer": "C",
      "explanationEn": "The investor’s interaction with corporate debt issuers is most common with their corporate treasury departments rather than more senior officials. In most cases, the parties dialogue about strategy, risk, financial structure (especially where the proposed debt sits in the debt hierarchy), and the covenants and protections for debt investors. Increasingly, however, dialogue about risk encompasses ESG matters, and debt investors are finding they can have some influence on the approach of fixed-income issuers.",
      "explanationZh": "投资者与公司债发行人的互动，最常见的是与其公司财务部门进行，而不是与更高层官员进行。多数情况下，各方会围绕战略、风险、财务结构（特别是拟发行债务在债务层级中的位置）以及债务投资者的契约条款和保护进行对话。然而，关于风险的对话越来越多地涵盖 ESG 事项，债务投资者也发现自己可以对固定收益发行人的做法产生一定影响。",
